{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0GE1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\tau \\to (\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0003": "$\\tau = fppf$", "OWNARGEND_0001": "]\n\\label{remark-no-fibre-products}\n", "REF_0001": "\\ref{examples-section-sheaves-locally-Noetherian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}[", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cd3a17d171d080cf5a233e2505b6e24931f4540cf16a7c0e8cafe0a43016b04e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:150cc2fe6622cca5fec8d6856720a6c8d53dc3ac4e8d398b43e169fc1073a39b", "source_text": "Warning<OWNARGEND_0001>The site <MATH_0001> does not have fibre products.\nHence we have to be careful in working with sheaves. For example,\nthe continuous inclusion functor\n<MATH_0002>\ndoes not define a morphism of sites. See\nExamples, Section <REF_0001>\nfor an example in case <MATH_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:edd71b7df1d7e9a8440a0003176d781f7670515ca6b86a86bf4bbbda4b11ee9b", "unit_id": "tag:0GE2:statement"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0GE1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : (\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\tau^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$X = \\lim X_i$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0005": "$F(X) = \\colim F(X_i)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:950673bb26648966ce9cea74594bd7ea797552603e5536938b2ac9acf7743c32", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:00c13bc0840ed32989723f2ee6585cd71a61898b7934d9b3fd1846b0ea688a5c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001>\nbe a functor. We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>limit preserving<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for any\ndirected limit of affine schemes <MATH_0003> of\n<MATH_0004> we have <MATH_0005>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f1cf8857f5ef978b881855b745b3a1c1ed7565c569e4edd74d3ba287da7afae9", "unit_id": "tag:0GE1:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0GE1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\tau \\in \\{Zariski, \\etale, smooth, syntomic, fppf\\}$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\tau \\to (\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\tau$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-canonical-extension}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:46da25b75be99791ff6bc340d6d9d5eda917de4f64a29ef549e6079d55e1a93d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:06bf4deda01e329c55067c1b0e3deb4831bdcfad5159e27e0cd55908d98aae50", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>.\nRestricting along the inclusion functor\n<MATH_0002>\ndefines an equivalence of categories between\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the category of limit preserving sheaves on\n<MATH_0003> and\n<STRUCT_0003> the category of limit preserving sheaves on\n<MATH_0004>\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6ad58efc00eb985b8b29f1df3874e4ab96706ad02dfeccf8464a0b2731eea0b7", "unit_id": "tag:0GE3:statement"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0GE1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : (\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\tau^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$F' : (\\Sch/S)_\\tau^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$F'$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-lemma-extend}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topologies-lemma-extend-sheaf-general}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{topologies-lemma-extend}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cd972236395e505f97913b062d25c3081c3ada8f1aaa1d55d5d77b73b1f1b6a2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1a96a55452fc2aa25ecf37f499b06cfe28a9d3b0a18c4caf7f5b18c5206b219d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a functor which is both limit preserving and a sheaf.\nBy Topologies, Lemmas\n<REF_0001> and <REF_0002>\nthere exists a unique functor\n<MATH_0002>\nwhich is limit preserving, a sheaf, and restricts to <MATH_0003>.\nIn fact, the construction of <MATH_0004> in\nTopologies, Lemma <REF_0003>\nis functorial in <MATH_0005> and this construction is a quasi-inverse\nto restriction. Some details omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:09a76211f7b0d3f14b7a41fb9f723ab34ada8841e72f663eecc59c2eb077ef44", "unit_id": "tag:0GE3:proof"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0GE1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0003": "$h_X : (\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\tau^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-representable-limit-preserving}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e42894e382d43628ec3784de22641ff026576c31e1f60c41ce977b2779b63b35", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b2f2862cfcc6c22beee3c0208da605c97d53068a6c353c5de803dee2d299c104", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an object of <MATH_0002>. If the functor\nof points <MATH_0003>\nis limit preserving, then <MATH_0004> is locally of finite presentation over <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7f17e00b764704c17b7dbc77fd394c23cfef74863a7597d9dff0825601bea995", "unit_id": "tag:0GE4:statement"}
